  "adaptation": {
    "mask": "Original foreground matte M, threshold 0.01 after resizing to native 64 by 64 grid.",
    "method": [
      "Compute baseline edit B as the soft-foreground velocity minus neutral velocity. Compute D as the whole-field stronger target minus the soft-foreground target.",
      "Within the support M > 0.01, let b = B and v = M times D. Remove the projection of v onto b to obtain tangent t.",
      "Let c = 1 - squared_norm(D) / (2 * squared_norm(b)). Replace b by c*b + sqrt((1-c)*(1+c)) * norm(b) * t/norm(t).",
      "Use the original baseline field outside the support and emit the same dtype."
    ],
    "halo": "The alternative uses a 5 by 5 max pool at stride one before thresholding, extending the mask by up to two latent sites.",
